{% comment %}
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SEO NOINDEX SNIPPET — Add to theme.liquid inside <head> tag
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Purpose: Prevents Google from indexing pages that waste crawl budget.
  This single snippet handles the noindex cases that redirects can't:

  1. Blog articles flagged via seo.noindex metafield (set by shopify-noindex.js)
  2. Blog tag archive pages (/blogs/<blog>/tagged/*)
  3. Paginated pages (page 2+)
  4. Search results, cart, account, checkout pages
  5. Collection filter/sort parameter URLs
  6. Product variant parameter URLs

  Collections hidden via seo.hidden (noindex-thin-collections.js) need no
  snippet: Shopify handles that metafield natively.

  INSTALLATION:
  1. Shopify Admin → Online Store → Themes → Edit Code
  2. Open layout/theme.liquid
  3. Paste this snippet AFTER the existing <meta> tags but BEFORE </head>
  4. Save and verify on the storefront (view source, search for "noindex")

  To revert: remove this snippet from theme.liquid.
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %} ── 1. Article-level noindex via metafield ── {% endcomment %}
{% if template contains 'article' %}
  {% if article.metafields.seo.noindex == 'true' %}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %} ── 2. Blog tag archive pages (always noindex) ── {% endcomment %}
{% if current_tags %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{% endif %}

{% comment %} ── 3. Paginated pages — page 2+ (always noindex) ── {% endcomment %}
{% if current_page > 1 %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{% endif %}

{% comment %} ── 4. Search, cart, account pages (always noindex) ── {% endcomment %}
{% if template contains 'search' or template == 'cart' %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{% endif %}
{% if request.path contains '/account' or request.path contains '/checkout' %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
{% endif %}

{% comment %} ── 5. Collection filter/sort parameter URLs ── {% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  When someone uses collection filters (?filter.v.price=, ?sort_by=, etc.)
  or collection + tag combos, noindex the result. The canonical collection
  page is all Google needs.
{% endcomment %}
{% if template contains 'collection' %}
  {% assign has_params = false %}
  {% if request.url contains '?' %}
    {% assign has_params = true %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if has_params %}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %} ── 6. Product variant parameter URLs ── {% endcomment %}
{% if template contains 'product' %}
  {% if request.url contains '?variant=' %}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
